        "fsm.go:181:285"
      ],
      "rationale": "The previously missing handoff is now available for inspection. leaderLoop receives commitCh, reads the accumulator's commit index and selects inflight futures only through that index. It keys groupFutures by each future's log.Index and passes lastIdxInGroup to processLogs. processLogs traverses the unapplied prefix through that limit, obtains each log from its indexed future or GetLog, and sends prepared tuples to fsmMutateCh. runFSM receives []*commitTuple and invokes applyBatch, which either uses applySingle or the BatchingFSM interface. Command responses remain associated with their tuple futures. This answers the missing-source and command-selection questions underlying the issue; it does not establish end-to-end correctness or automatically confirm the graph relation.",
      "residual_issue_ids": [],
      "scope_limitations": [
        "This resolution establishes the structure of the normal leader handoff through static source inspection.",
        "Replication durability, admissible membership histories and execution-level command correlation require separate evidence."
      ]
