      ],
      "explanation": "The Apply document expressly promises durable quorum storage before FSM application. The FSM interface separately requires majority commitment before Apply, and BatchingFSM describes batches as committed before delivery. These statements establish the goal's applicability independently of the accumulator implementation. The API's leadership-loss uncertainty and restore abortion qualify client outcomes without withdrawing the ordinary commitment-before-application expectation.",
      "alternatives": "Single-command and batched application are alternative delivery mechanisms with the same relevant commitment prerequisite. Follower application may lag without contradicting this goal.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "The goal could fail while accumulator arithmetic remains correct if reports misrepresent stored prefixes or the delivery path selects an unsupported command. Applicability does not establish that those failures occur.",
      "limitations": [
        "The concrete storage contract and applicable storage implementation remain unestablished.",
        "Complete obligation coverage for normal command delivery remains outstanding."
      ]
    },
    {
      "scope_limitations": [
        "The obligation concerns advancements within one commitment instance, not retrospective support under later configurations."
      ],
      "target_id": "O_commit",
      "aspect": "applicability",
