      "explanation": "Constructor, report acceptance, voter replacement and recalculation cover the accumulator's stated transition responsibilities. The ascending order statistic at (n-1)/2 expresses strict-majority reported support for nonempty voter sets; the advancement guards express monotonicity and the instance threshold. Caller code establishes a local report after successful StoreLogs and installs a new voter configuration after dispatching its configuration entry. The downstream path now explains how the accumulator contributes to delivery, without making these additional responsibilities part of O_commit.",
      "alternatives": "Remote non-pipelined replication, pipeline progress, snapshot progress and local writes require their respective producer contracts. Maintaining an old committed index is distinct from making a new advancement.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "Incorrect remote evidence, an inadmissible transition or incorrect log selection could violate G_apply while O_commit holds. Therefore the selected obligation is sufficient only for its stated local advancement question.",
