      ],
      "explanation": "The G_apply-to-O_commit direction and necessary-component interpretation of depends_all are supported. The previously missing implementation link is now visible: commitCh leads to reading the accumulator index; inflight selection stops beyond that index; groupFutures retains log-index identity; processLogs prepares tuples through the selected limit; and runFSM dispatches those tuples to single or batched application. This supports the relation's stated contribution without treating it as a complete proof of G_apply.",
      "alternatives": "Followers call processLogs with no futures after advancing from LeaderCommitIndex. The FSM can apply individual commands or batches. Shutdown and restoration are explicit alternative branches, not evidence of guaranteed eventual normal delivery.",
      "counterexample_reasoning": "Even with correct accumulator advancements, false input evidence or a separate delivery-selection failure could violate the goal. The source chain answers the two reading issues but does not discharge those responsibilities.",
